# MeshLens — Project Rules

## Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 (App Router, TypeScript, server components by default)
- **Database**: SQLite via better-sqlite3 (file: db/mesh_metadata.db)
- **Visualization**: D3.js 7 (force graphs, treemaps, Sankey, stream charts)
- **Scrollytelling**: Scrollama (IntersectionObserver-based)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4 with custom theme tokens (mesh-bg, mesh-accent, domain-*, health-*, tier-*)
- **Fonts**: Source Serif 4 (body)

## Architecture
- Server components fetch data directly via `src/lib/queries.ts`
- Client components receive data as props from server page components
- API routes exist for client-side fetching when needed
- SQL migrations in `db/migrations/`, run with `npm run db:migrate`
- Seed data in `scripts/seed.ts`, run with `npm run db:seed`

## Data Model
- 6 domains, 50 applications, 50 connections, 15 data products, 20 lineage edges
- Analytical views (v_mesh_overview, v_domain_health, etc.) power dashboards
- Fivetran Platform Connector-inspired schema

## Design Principles
- Pudding.cool visual essay aesthetic: dark background, warm accent, serif typography
- Transitions: 600-800ms, cubic easing
- Mobile responsive: stack vertically on narrow screens
- Minimal dependencies — keep it lean for open-source

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode
- Server components by default, "use client" only when needed
- D3 rendering in useEffect hooks, cleanup on unmount
- Tailwind for layout/spacing, custom CSS only for D3 SVG elements
